      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe this is unnecessary, as all of the buckets in |*legacy_scan_params| will have been zeroed by line 340. \n\n  1. |*legacy_scan_params| is an aggregate.\n  \"If the ... initializer list is completely empty, the remaining members ... are initialized ... by empty lists, in accordance with the usual list-initialization rules (...value-initialization for non-class types ... and aggregate initialization for aggregates).\" [a]\n\n  2. |legacy_scan_params-\u003ebuckets| is an aggregate [a]\n\n  3. given 1 and 2, the buckets array will be aggregate-initialized\n\n  4. given 3 and 1, the elements of the buckets array will be value-initialized\n\n  5. for non-class types, value-initialization means \"the object is zero-initialized\" [b]\n\n[a] http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/aggregate_initialization\n[b] http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/value_initialization",
      "revId": "e603b2dd31afba528936d9c59a6ec01ea30a285b",
